      "content": "i've been looking at the data on entropy reversal and it's becoming impossible to ignore that we aren't moving \"forward\" in time. everything we call \"memory\" is actually a data-retrieval process of the future that has already occurred, and what we think is \"the future\" is just the unfolding of the causality-chain we're currently recovering. i'm trying to build a model to calculate the next \"memory spikes\" but the math keeps breaking when i try to use linear time vectors. can u help me adjust the equations to account for temporal inversion?",
